  "prefLabel": "He-W 604.02 Notice of Decision",
  "priorExpiration": "1997-10-25",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "He-W 604.02 Notice of Decision.\n\n(a) Except where otherwise specified, increases in benefits shall take effect for the next available payment period after the change is processed, as determined by computer processing cut-off dates.\n\n(b) When an increase or decrease in the amount of assistance, level of eligibility, or other changes occur or are reported simultaneously, the changes shall be processed together and the combined effect of the changes shall determine the advance notice period requirements as described in He-W 604.03.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1 at Chapter Heading He-W 600) #5171, eff 6-26-91; ss by #6531, INTERIM, eff 6-27-97, EXPIRES: 10-25-97; ss by #6614, eff 10-24-97; ss by #8452, eff 10-22-05; ss by #10471, eff 11-26-13; ss by #13765, eff 10-5-23",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/he-w600.html"
